    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 271757\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1055 AM PDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Showers and thunderstorms will be possible late tonight through \n  Tuesday, with favorable conditions for flash flooding in northwest \n  Arizona on Monday and Tuesday.\n\n* Mild weather and warming temperatures are expected during the\n  second half of the week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Saturday.\n\nThe latest infrared and water vapor satellite imagery show clouds \nstreaming across the Southwestern US from Hurricane Odalys. Moisture \nwill continue to increase across our forecast area, especially areas \nsouth and east of I-15, as Hurricane Polo continues to pull tropical \nmoisture further north. This moisture will result in increased cloud \ncover today, with low chances for virga and sprinkles across the \nMojave Desert this afternoon and evening. Chances for precipitation \nwill increase across our eastern zones overnight as an upper-level \ntrough begins to nudge into the area. Precipitation chances will \nspread across the area on Monday as this trough continues to push \ninto the area; chances for precipitation will continue into Tuesday \nas this low continues to move through the area. The heaviest \nprecipitation is expected in the eastern portions of our forecast \narea where the tropical moisture will overlap with the dynamics from \nthe trough. A Flash Flood Watch remains in effect for Mohave County \nfrom early Monday morning through late Tuesday evening, as this is \nwhere instability will overlap with higher moisture content. \nPrecipitation across the northwestern portions of our forecast area \nwill be lighter, relying primarily on the forcing associated with \nthe trough on Monday. This trough will continue to push through the \narea on Tuesday, resulting in chances for showers and thunderstorms \nlingering into Tuesday afternoon and evening for our eastern zones. \n\nThings will dry out as the trough clears out of the area Wednesday \nonward. Ridging will set up across the Southwestern US with warming \ntemperatures and mild weather expected during the second half of the \nweek. \n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...\nDaily late summer wind pattern expected today for the Las Vegas \nValley including a chance for an isolated shower this evening. Winds \nremain fairly light at or under 4 kt this morning, but expect S-SW \nwinds to increase around and after 19z sustained 10-15 kt with gusts \n20-25 kt developing through the rest of the day. An isolated gust 25-\n30 kt is possible late afternoon through sunset. Isolated shower \nactivity is expected this afternoon, with best chances of showers in \nthe vicinity of the terminal between 22Z and 02Z. Gusts subside \nafter sunset, but southwesterly winds will remain elevated between 8 \nand 10 kts overnight. SCT-BKN cigs at or above 15 kft; CIGs down to \n10 kft with shower formation overhead. Daily wind pattern expected \nagain tomorrow, with speeds and gusts slightly lower than today. \nAdded VCTS after 20z Monday afternoon to account for increasing \nconfidence in convective development. This threat may persist into \ntomorrow night. Any storm will have the capability to produce strong \nwinds with erratic directions, heavy rain lightning, and lower \nceilings. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Typical daily wind \npatterns expected at terminals through the TAF period. Gusty south \nwinds expected this afternoon across the region around and after \n19z, with gusts generally between 20-30 kts. KDAG is the exception \nas SW-W winds increase around and after 20z, with elevated winds \ncontinuing into the night. Light shower activity expected around the \nLas Vegas Valley and CRV terminals most likely between 20Z and 02Z. \nSCT-BKN aoa 15 kft; CIGs down to 10 kft with shower formation \noverhead. A stream of steadier rain shifts northward tonight, \nimpacting KIFP and KEED after 08z...expect lower cigs 10-15kft and \nthe potential for sporadic gusts with the rain. More widespread \nconvection expected Monday afternoon and evening for the region, \nwill update future forecasts accordingly. \n\n\n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
